      "title": "Trapped-ion quantum computer simulates a classic quantum interference effect",
      "summary": "Researchers used a hybrid trapped-ion quantum computer to simulate the Aharonov-Bohm effect, in which particles are affected by a field they never touch, inside a model of a lattice gauge theory. This shows that today's machines can mimic the physics of fundamental forces in a controlled way. The simulation is small, though, and far from the larger systems needed to answer open physics questions.",
